+# Terminology correction: formation, participation and responsibility
+
+7 October 2026, Asia/Bangkok. Ren's messages below are preserved verbatim. The context and application note are AI-authored.
+
+## Ren's words
+
+> authorship what is authorship doing in our theory? if it is doing something important, then this name may not be appropriate
+
+After the assistant explained that the recent term bundled formation history, participation and ethical responsibility, and proposed naming those relations directly, Ren replied:
+
+> yes, please fix all
+
+Ren then extended the request:
+
+> for poor words in the repo, replace them too
+
+## Scope of the correction
+
+This authorizes a contextual language revision. The shared account should explain how activities and differentiated positions form and change the conditions of further activity. Historical contribution, actual participation, effective choice and justified responsibility are related questions whose answers must not be supplied by one ambiguous label.
+
+The correction preserves actual differentiated effects, legitimate choice and the need to justify normative conclusions. It does not establish universal ethics, remove the capacities described by an older term, or authorize changing quotations and source originals. Documentary authorship, attributed philosophical terminology and names identifying existing formal declarations retain their provenance and scope.
+
+The [shared method](../../theories/shengsheng-buxi-generative-existence/unified-2026-10-05/NONDUAL-METHOD.md#formation-participation-and-responsibility) records the current formulation. The [revision record](../../_process/research/2026-10-05-generative-foundation-review/root-foundation/LANGUAGE-AND-FORMATION-CORRECTION.md) distinguishes terminology changes from new research claims.
